# EAS Build ignore — keeps the upload focused on the Expo app.
#
# Why this exists:
# Without this file, EAS uploads the entire pnpm workspace and runs
#   `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` at the repo root. That fails with
#     EACCES: permission denied, mkdir 'artifacts/api-server/node_modules'
# because the EAS Linux worker can't symlink workspace deps into peer
# package node_modules.
#
# Strategy:
# - Keep pnpm-workspace.yaml so EAS detects pnpm (not yarn) and so pnpm can
#   resolve the `catalog:` versions used by the Expo app.
# - Drop pnpm-lock.yaml. The lockfile lists every workspace importer
#   (api-server, voycelab-landing, etc.). Once those packages are removed
#   from the upload, --frozen-lockfile would fail with "lockfile out of sync".
#   The eas-build-pre-install hook in artifacts/square-voice-agent regenerates
#   a clean lockfile against the slimmed-down workspace before EAS runs its
#   own install.
# - Drop the unrelated workspace artifacts and libraries.
# - Drop dev-only env files, caches, build outputs, and tooling.

# Force a clean, partial-workspace install on EAS workers
pnpm-lock.yaml

# Other workspace artifacts (server, web, PWA) — not used by the Expo app
artifacts/api-server/
artifacts/voycelab-landing/
artifacts/voice-agent-pwa/

# Server-only libraries (square-voice-agent has zero @workspace/* deps)
lib/

# Caches and build outputs
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/.expo/
**/.next/
**/.cache/

# Local environment and secrets
.env
.env.*

# Tooling
.git/
.cursor/
.claude/
.vscode/

# Logs and OS junk
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Repo-level docs / scripts unused by the Expo build
CLAUDE.md
RAILWAY.md
README.md
railway.json
nixpacks.toml
start-all.bat
tsconfig.base.json
tsconfig.json
scripts/
